# Toyota Aygo X five-door crossover, 2022 onwards.
#
# The Aygo X: the raised city-car crossover with the narrow upper grille,
# the large lower intake, the black wheel-arch cladding and the high tail.
# It replaced the Aygo hatch in 2022.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Toyota_Aygo_X
#
# Dimensions 3.700 x 1.740 x 1.525 m, wheelbase 2.430 m (published Aygo X
# figures; the reference pack itself does not print a dimension table).
#
# Shape reference: NO level side profile exists. Image 1 is an elevated rear
# oblique and the most side-on view found; the flank is estimated and the
# limitation is recorded.
#
# Colours: grade (a), the Toyota UK Aygo X brochure of May 2022 (GBNGV-AYGOX):
# Pure White, Silver Metallic, Eclipse Black and Juniper Blue. Weights 9, 8,
# 7, 6, total 30, provisional.
#
# Speed 170 km/h. Comfort 65/280, on the line 180 + 1.5 x 65. Classes 0,1.
# Dates are road presence: 2022 intro, retires staggered 2042-2045.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/toyota-aygo-x.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/toyota-aygo-x.dae. References:
# citycars/references/toyota-aygo-x/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted deviations: the flank is estimated from the oblique image, because no
# level side elevation exists. Pre-facelift petrol body. The black roof and
# hatch treatment are fixed, not the grade-specific two-tone layouts. Lamp
# wraps and cladding contours are simplified, and the front lamp edges are
# more angular than the photographs.


obj=citycar
name=ToyotaAygoX(PureWhite)
copyright=JamesPetts

DistributionWeight=9
